+The transmit queue has four 1024-byte frames. At most 16 bytes are sent per background pass, limited by \texttt{availableForWrite()}. Periodic telemetry is queued only while two slots remain free, leaving room for acknowledgments and events. A command that changes state is not run unless its acknowledgment can be queued. After congestion, the client must time out and resynchronize; an unacknowledged command cannot be assumed to have run.
+
+When the lease expires, OFF and enable inhibition are requested first. The lease is then disarmed, streaming is stopped, and an event is marked pending. Flash is not saved. Reconnection requires a new lease and explicit ON. This guard runs in the background loop; it does not disconnect mains, discharge capacitors, or replace an independent hardware interlock.
 
